{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     navbar/search — a button shaped like a field.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     data-ghost-search is GHOST'S hook. Ghost injects its own search script
     (Sodo Search) through {{ghost_head}} and binds any element carrying that
     attribute; the modal, the index and the keyboard shortcut are all
     Ghost's. The theme supplies no search of its own — see abstract/README's
     rule, this is the "does Ghost already do it" case exactly.

     A BUTTON, NOT AN INPUT. Typing happens in Ghost's modal, and a real text
     field here would take focus, get typed into, and do nothing.

     The ⌘K hint is Ghost's own binding, so the kbd is a statement of fact
     rather than a promise this theme has to keep.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<button type="button" class="ns-navsearch" data-ghost-search aria-label="{{t "Search"}}">
    {{> "icons/magnifying-glass"}}
    <span class="ns-navsearch__text">{{t "Search"}}</span>
    <kbd class="ns-navsearch__kbd">⌘K</kbd>
</button>
